# Construction Business Expense Tracker - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview

This is a Progressive Web App (PWA) for construction business expense and income tracking built with Nuxt 4, Firebase, and modern UI components. The app is optimized for mobile-first design with receipt photo processing and financial management capabilities.

## Tech Stack & Architecture

### Core Framework

- **Nuxt 4+** (latest stable version with Turbo Mode)
- **Vue 3.3+** with Composition API
- **TypeScript** for type safety
- **PWA** capabilities for mobile installation
- **Nuxt/VueUse** for any functionality that exists on their library
- **Nuxt/UI** as the primary UI component library

### UI & Design System

- **Nuxt/UI v4+** as the primary UI component library
- **Tailwind CSS** for styling but please follow Nuxt UI standard
- **Modern Card Layout** design pattern
- **Mobile-first** responsive design
- **Professional but modern** aesthetic
- **Accent colors** for financial categories
- **Dark/Light mode** support for different lighting conditions

### Backend & Services

- **Firebase Authentication** for user management
- **Firestore** for real-time financial data
- **Firebase Storage** for receipt images (5-year auto-delete)
- **Firebase Functions** for receipt OCR processing
- **Firebase Hosting** for deployment

## Core Features

### Receipt Processing

- **Camera integration** for receipt photos
- **OCR processing** to extract expense data
- **Automatic categorization** of expenses
- **Multi-item splitting** from single receipts
- **Credit card number detection** from receipts

### Financial Management

- **Manual expense/income entry** as fallback
- **Project-based budgeting** with spending limits
- **Account tracking** (credit cards, debit cards, bank accounts, loans)
- **Real-time budget monitoring** with "Amount left to spend"
- **5-year auto-delete** policy for receipt images

### Reporting & Analytics

- **Time-based reports** (year, month, day, custom)
- **Category breakdown** analysis
- **Payment source tracking** by account
- **Income vs expense** comparisons
- **Project budget** performance tracking

## Development Guidelines

### Component Guidelines

1. **Always use Nuxt/UI components** as the foundation
2. **Create custom components** for financial-specific features
3. **Use TypeScript interfaces** for all financial data structures
4. **Follow Vue 3 Composition API** patterns
5. **Implement proper error handling** for financial operations
6. **Leverage already made VueUse composable** to unnecessary code

### Firebase Integration

1. **Use Firebase composables** for authentication state
2. **Implement proper error handling** for all Firebase operations
3. **Use TypeScript interfaces** for Firestore document types
4. **Implement offline-first** data patterns for financial data
5. **Use Firebase Security Rules** for financial data protection
6. **Implement auto-delete** for receipt images after 5 years

### PWA Requirements

1. **Service Worker** for offline functionality
2. **App manifest** for installation prompts
3. **Responsive design** for all screen sizes
4. **Touch-friendly** interface elements
5. **Fast loading** and smooth animations
6. **Camera access** for receipt photos

### Design System

1. **Card-based Layout** for financial data display
2. **Category color coding** for expense types
3. **Progress indicators** for budget tracking
4. **Professional typography** for financial data
5. **Consistent spacing** using Tailwind utilities
6. **Dark/Light mode** toggle for different environments

### Mobile-First Approach

1. **Touch targets** minimum 44px
2. **Swipe gestures** for navigation
3. **Pull-to-refresh** functionality
4. **Bottom navigation** for primary actions
5. **Responsive typography** scaling
6. **Camera integration** for receipt capture

## Financial Data Models

### Expense Interface

```typescript
interface IExpense {
  id: string;
  amount: number;
  category: string;
  projectId: string;
  accountId: string;
  receiptImageUrl?: string;
  description: string;
  date: Date;
  isManualEntry: boolean;
  ocrData?: IOcrResult;
}
```

### Project Interface

```typescript
interface IProject {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  budget: number;
  spent: number;
  startDate: Date;
  endDate?: Date;
  status: "active" | "completed" | "paused";
}
```

### Account Interface

```typescript
interface IAccount {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  type: "credit" | "debit" | "bank" | "loan";
  lastFourDigits?: string;
  isActive: boolean;
}
```

## Security & Privacy

- **Financial data encryption** in transit and at rest
- **Receipt image security** with automatic deletion
- **User data isolation** per account
- **Secure OCR processing** without data retention
- **GDPR compliance** for data handling

## Performance Optimization

- **Lazy loading** for receipt images
- **Image compression** for storage efficiency
- **Offline data sync** for financial records
- **Efficient OCR processing** with queuing
- **Cached financial calculations** for reports

Remember: Always prioritize financial data accuracy, use Nuxt/UI components, and maintain a professional aesthetic suitable for business financial management with dark/light mode support.
